#: ../../index.rst:118
msgid "Get started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:121
msgid "Download the archive for our system from the `latest release <download_>`_, put ``guidedog`` on the ``PATH``, and create a project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:124
msgid ""
"guidedog quickstart docs\n"
"guidedog build html docs\n"
"guidedog build pdf docs\n"
"guidedog serve docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:131
msgid "``quickstart`` writes ``conf.toml``, ``index.rst``, and templates we can edit. ``serve`` rebuilds the site while we write. The `tutorial <manual-tutorial_>`_ walks through a first project. To build Guidedog from source, install Rust and follow the `instructions in the repository <build_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:137
msgid "Design discussions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:140
msgid "Guidedog's design decisions are written down as numbered discussions: the problem, the alternatives, the decision, and the evidence. We can read each one on the web or download it as a PDF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:144
msgid "Our own project can keep its discussions the same way, with ``guidedog dsc``. The `manual <manual-discussions_>`_ shows how."
msgstr ""

